@using MartenStudio.Services.Health
@using MartenStudio.Services.Schema
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@using PostgresStudio.Components.Shared
@using PostgresStudio.Services
@using PostgresStudio.Services.Health
@using PostgresStudio.Services.Schema
@implements IDisposable
@inject ISchemaDataService SchemaData
@inject StudioState State
@inject IHealthService Health
@inject IOptions<MartenStudioOptions> Options
@inject ILogger<IndexesTab> Logger

@*
    Both directions of the join: what Postgres has that the configuration does not ask for, and what the
    configuration asks for that Postgres does not have. Every suggestion is a StoreOptions line, never
    DDL - an index the studio created directly would be one the host's own configuration knows nothing
    about, and the next apply would drop it again. Not "AutoCreate.All would": CreateOrUpdate drops it,
    because Weasel writes "drop index" for every index on a Marten table that the configuration does not
    declare and reports the table as Update (packet P7-fix, finding B2).

    Nothing on this tab asks the database for anything but pg_catalog rows: the declarations come from
    StoreOptions through SchemaDeclarationReader, never from AllObjects().

    "A table Marten manages" is wider than the document and event tables (DB-7): a flat-table projection's
    table and every StoreOptions.Storage.ExtendedSchemaObjects table are migrated by an apply too - Marten
    yields ExtendedSchemaObjects as a feature of its own - so their undeclared indexes are dropped like any
    other, and this tab says so. It used to call them "not a Marten table" that "no migration from here
    touches", which is exactly the wording hard rule 14 forbids. A table this store does not declare is
    "unmanaged" - a statement about what the studio can see, never a promise that an apply leaves it alone.

    An index on a partition is never listed (it is named after the partition, and a Marten partition is
    named after its tenant), and neither is anything on a hidden document type's table. A definition that
    names a schema this visitor may not see - an expression index calling a function there - reads
    ‹withheld› in its place, as the database browser's object detail does. A registered store that cannot
    be read withholds the indexes of every table it could own, with a notice, rather than blanking the tab.

    The invalid, redundant and unused marks (F6) are the health advisor's own findings T03, T04 and T05 from
    its last sweep, read through the cache-only CachedFindingsAsync: the tab never starts a sweep, and with
    nothing cached it draws no mark at all - an absent mark is never a claim that an index is fine. Each mark
    links to its finding on the Health page.

    A pgvector HNSW or IVFFlat index - Marten.PgVector's VectorIndex<T>() makes one, over an expression on the
    document table - says under its definition what pg_get_indexdef only implies: each column's operator class and
    the distance it serves, and m, ef_construction or lists from reloptions, with pgvector's default where the index
    sets none (VectorIndexSummary).
*@

@if (!loading && indexes.ClassificationNotice is { Length: > 0 } notice)
{
    <div class="ms-alert ms-alert-warning ms-schema-degraded" role="status">
        <div class="ms-alert-content">
            <p>@notice</p>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@if (loading)
{
    <LoadingSpinner />
}
else if (indexes.Reason is { Length: > 0 } reason)
{
    <ErrorAlert Message="@reason" OnRetry="LoadAsync" RetryText="@(indexes.Busy ? "Try again" : "Retry")" />
}
else
{
    <div class="ms-schema-summary">
        <span><strong>@indexes.Indexes.Count</strong> indexes</span>
        <span><strong>@indexes.NeverUsedCount</strong> never scanned</span>
        <span><strong>@indexes.Missing.Count</strong> declared but missing</span>
        <span><strong>@indexes.Unindexed.Count</strong> collections with only a primary key</span>
        @if (MarkedCount("T03") is > 0 and var invalid)
        {
            <span class="ms-schema-health-count ms-schema-health-count-invalid"><strong>@invalid</strong> invalid</span>
        }
        @if (MarkedCount("T04") is > 0 and var redundant)
        {
            <span class="ms-schema-health-count"><strong>@redundant</strong> redundant</span>
        }
    </div>

    @if (HasMarks)
    {
        <p class="ms-schema-note ms-schema-health-note">
            The invalid, redundant and unused marks are the health advisor's, from its last check
            @(marksMeasuredAt is { } at ? "(" + State.FormatInSelectedTimeZone(at) + ")" : string.Empty); each links to
            the finding, with what it is based on and what to change.
        </p>
    }

    @if (indexes.WouldBeDroppedCount > 0)
    {
        <div class="ms-alert ms-alert-error" role="alert">
            <div class="ms-alert-content">
                <p>
                    <strong>@DroppedHeadline</strong>
                    They exist on tables Marten manages - its document and event tables, and the
                    projections' and <code>ExtendedSchemaObjects</code>' tables it migrates for the
                    application - and nothing declares them, so Weasel writes <code>drop index</code> for
                    each - under <code>AutoCreate.CreateOrUpdate</code>, not only under <code>All</code>.
                    Declare them, or name each one in <code>opts.Schema.For&lt;T&gt;().IgnoreIndex("...")</code>
                    (<code>opts.Events.IgnoreIndex("...")</code> on an event table, and
                    <code>table.IgnoreIndex("...")</code> on a projection's or an extended table).
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    }

    @if (indexes.Missing.Count > 0)
    {
        <h2 class="ms-section-title">Declared but missing</h2>
        <p class="ms-schema-note">
            The store's configuration asks for these and the database does not have them. The Drift tab
            will show the same thing as pending changes.
        </p>
        <TableScroll Label="Declared but missing indexes table">
            <table class="ms-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Index</th>
                        <th>Table</th>
                        <th>Collection</th>
                        <th>Would be created as</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (MissingIndex missing in indexes.Missing)
                    {
                        <tr class="ms-table-row" @key="missing.Schema + missing.Table + missing.Name">
                            <td class="ms-table-cell ms-table-cell-mono">@missing.Name</td>
                            <td class="ms-table-cell ms-table-cell-mono">@(missing.Schema + "." + missing.Table)</td>
                            <td class="ms-table-cell ms-table-cell-mono">@missing.CollectionAlias</td>
                            <td class="ms-table-cell ms-index-definition">@missing.Definition</td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </TableScroll>
    }

    @if (indexes.Unindexed.Count > 0)
    {
        <h2 class="ms-section-title">Collections with only a primary key</h2>
        <p class="ms-schema-note">
            Every filter on one of these is a sequential scan over the whole table. Each line below is the
            <code>StoreOptions</code> registration that would add an index, in the order worth trying them:
            a computed index on the property being filtered, a duplicated column when that property is
            also sorted or joined on, a GIN index for containment queries across the whole document, and
            the <code>mt_last_modified</code> index that only helps a "recently changed" listing.
        </p>

        @foreach (UnindexedCollection collection in indexes.Unindexed)
        {
            <div class="ms-config-card" @key="collection.QualifiedName">
                <div class="ms-config-card-header">
                    <h3 class="ms-config-card-title">@collection.Alias</h3>
                    <span class="ms-config-card-subtitle">@collection.QualifiedName</span>
                </div>
                <div class="ms-config-card-body">
                    <ul class="ms-suggestion-list">
                        @foreach (string suggestion in collection.Suggestions)
                        {
                            <li @key="suggestion"><code class="ms-suggestion-line">@suggestion</code></li>
                        }
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        }
    }

    <h2 class="ms-section-title">Indexes in the database</h2>

    @if (indexes.Indexes.Count == 0)
    {
        <div class="ms-empty">
            <p class="ms-empty-title">No indexes</p>
            <p class="ms-empty-description">Nothing has been created yet in this store's schemas.</p>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <TableScroll Label="Indexes table">
            <table class="ms-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Index</th>
                        <th>Table</th>
                        <th>Flags</th>
                        <th class="ms-num">Size</th>
                        <th class="ms-num">Scans</th>
                        <th class="ms-num">Tuples read</th>
                        <th>Definition</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (IndexInfo index in indexes.Indexes)
                    {
                        <tr class="ms-table-row" @key="index.Schema + index.Table + index.Name">
                            <td class="ms-table-cell ms-table-cell-mono">@index.Name</td>
                            <td class="ms-table-cell ms-table-cell-mono">
                                @(index.Schema + "." + index.Table)
                                @if (index.CollectionAlias is { Length: > 0 } alias)
                                {
                                    <span class="ms-index-flag">@alias</span>
                                }
                            </td>
                            <td class="ms-table-cell">
                                @if (index.IsPrimaryKey)
                                {
                                    <span class="ms-index-flag">primary key</span>
                                }
                                @if (index.IsUnique && !index.IsPrimaryKey)
                                {
                                    <span class="ms-index-flag">unique</span>
                                }
                                @if (index.WouldBeDropped)
                                {
                                    <span class="ms-index-flag ms-index-flag-danger">would be dropped</span>
                                }
                                else if (index.IgnoredByConfiguration)
                                {
                                    <span class="ms-index-flag ms-index-flag-info">ignored by config</span>
                                }
                                else if (!index.DeclaredByMarten && !index.OnMartenTable)
                                {
                                    <span class="ms-index-flag ms-index-flag-info"
                                          title="This store's configuration does not declare the table, as far as the studio can see.">unmanaged table</span>
                                }
                                @if (index.NeverUsed && !index.IsConstraint)
                                {
                                    <span class="ms-index-flag ms-index-flag-warn">never used</span>
                                }
                                @foreach (IndexHealthMark mark in MarksFor(index))
                                {
                                    <a class="@MarkClass(mark)" href="@mark.Link" title="@mark.Title" data-code="@mark.Code" @key="mark.Code">@mark.Label</a>
                                }
                            </td>
                            <td class="ms-table-cell ms-num">@SchemaFormat.Bytes(index.Bytes)</td>
                            <td class="ms-table-cell ms-num">@SchemaFormat.Count(index.Scans)</td>
                            <td class="ms-table-cell ms-num">@SchemaFormat.Count(index.TuplesRead)</td>
                            <td class="ms-table-cell">
                                <div class="ms-index-definition">@index.Definition</div>
                                @if (index.Vector is { } vector)
                                {
                                    <VectorIndexSummary Model="vector" />
                                }
                                @if (index.Suggestion is { Length: > 0 } suggestion)
                                {
                                    <p class="ms-suggestion">@suggestion</p>
                                }
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </TableScroll>
    }
}

@code {
    private readonly CancellationTokenSource lifetime = new();

    private SchemaIndexes indexes = SchemaIndexes.Empty;
    private bool loading = true;

    private IReadOnlyDictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<IndexHealthMark>> marks =
        new Dictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<IndexHealthMark>>();

    private DateTimeOffset? marksMeasuredAt;

    private IReadOnlyList<IndexHealthMark> MarksFor(IndexInfo index) =>
        marks.TryGetValue(SchemaKey.For(index.Schema, index.Table, index.Name), out IReadOnlyList<IndexHealthMark>? found) ? found : [];

    /// <summary>Whether any row on this tab carries a mark - a finding about no row here (a table's partitions) draws nothing.</summary>
    private bool HasMarks
    {
        get
        {
            foreach (IndexInfo index in indexes.Indexes)
            {
                if (MarksFor(index).Count > 0)
                {
                    return true;
                }
            }

            return false;
        }
    }

    private int MarkedCount(string code)
    {
        int count = 0;
        foreach (IndexInfo index in indexes.Indexes)
        {
            foreach (IndexHealthMark mark in MarksFor(index))
            {
                if (mark.Code == code)
                {
                    count++;
                }
            }
        }

        return count;
    }

    private static string MarkClass(IndexHealthMark mark) =>
        "ms-index-flag ms-schema-health-mark " + (mark.Severity == HealthSeverity.Critical ? "ms-index-flag-danger" : "ms-index-flag-warn");

    /// <summary>
    /// The advisor's marks for this scope, from its last sweep only. A failure here is never the tab's: the marks
    /// are a decoration, and the index list stands without them.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task LoadMarksAsync(StudioScope scope)
    {
        try
        {
            IReadOnlyList<HealthReportFinding> findings = await Health.CachedFindingsAsync(scope, SchemaHealthMarks.IndexCodes, lifetime.Token);

            marks = SchemaHealthMarks.ForIndexes(findings, finding => HealthLinks.ToFinding(Options.Value, scope, finding));
            marksMeasuredAt = findings.Count == 0 ? null : findings.Max(static x => x.Finding.MeasuredAt);
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException)
        {
        }
        catch (Exception exception)
        {
            // Debug: the marks decorate the list, which stands without them; nothing the visitor asked for failed.
            if (Logger.IsEnabled(LogLevel.Debug))
            {
                Logger.LogDebug(exception, "Marten Studio could not read the health advisor's cached findings for the Indexes tab");
            }

            marks = new Dictionary<string, IReadOnlyList<IndexHealthMark>>();
            marksMeasuredAt = null;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The headline of the drop warning, as one string.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Composed here rather than out of three markup expressions so that the rendered sentence is one
    /// run of text - which is what a test can assert on, and what a screen reader reads as a sentence.
    /// </remarks>
    private string DroppedHeadline => indexes.WouldBeDroppedCount == 1
        ? "1 index would be dropped by an apply."
        : $"{indexes.WouldBeDroppedCount} indexes would be dropped by an apply.";

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() => await LoadAsync();

    private async Task LoadAsync()
    {
        loading = true;
        await InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

        try
        {
            StudioScope? scope = State.ActiveScope;
            indexes = scope is null
                ? SchemaIndexes.Empty
                : await SchemaData.IndexesAsync(scope, lifetime.Token);

            if (scope is not null && indexes.Reason is null)
            {
                await LoadMarksAsync(scope);
            }
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException)
        {
        }
        catch (Exception exception)
        {
            indexes = SchemaIndexes.Unavailable(exception.Message);
        }
        finally
        {
            loading = false;
            await InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
        }
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        lifetime.Cancel();
        lifetime.Dispose();
    }
}
